"Everybody dies. Life is not a substance, like water or rock;, it's a process, like
fire or a wave crashing on the shore. It's a process that begins, lasts for a while, and ultimately ends.
Long or short, our moments are brief against the expanse of eternity.
- Sean Corroll, the big picture.

an opening.

Cat.
It was a recurring word, when the mind would go blank, that would just come to her. Cat, cat, cat, cat. Even blank minded in work chats she would pause, stare off, and type "Cat" as if was the perfectly most natural next word in the sentence, which it certainly never was.

Driving down the 405, she wondered if he controlled the world. He alwys said they would have money, and now here they were with money. He would predict what songs were going to be his favorites